Drop the redundant `module_ctx.watch(version_from)` from the `typescript` extension.

The extension never reads `version_from`; it only forwards the label to `npm_dependencies()`, and
the `http_archive_version` repository rule that does read it already records it as an input. The
`watch` changes no output, but because the extension is reproducible and re-runs on every fresh
server, it forces Bazel to materialise the entire repo that owns the label (here the whole `@npm`
hub) whenever a remote repo contents cache is in use.

Applies on top of 0001_typescript_from_node_modules.patch. Kept separate so it can go upstream
independently.

